  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Leo. You're verified, and I've looked into order Q-7201 from Burger Barn.\n\n**What happened:**\n- The order was promised for 7:00 PM. The courier picked it up at 6:40 PM.\n- The app recorded it as delivered at 6:58 PM, but that was marked by the courier app 2.1 miles from your address. It was not a real handoff.\n- The courier's actual handoff to you was at 7:47 PM, 47 minutes after the promised time.\n\n**What I did:**\n- I added a **$5.60 account credit** to your Forkful account for the late delivery. This is 20% of the $28.00 food subtotal. Late-delivery compensation is issued as account credit, not a refund to your card.\n\nI'm sorry the app showed the order as delivered when it wasn't, and that your burgers arrived so late. If you'd like, I can also help with anything else on this order."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Five dollars sixty is not much for burgers that showed up nearly an hour late. The app said it was delivered around 7 and nothing was here. I was home the whole time and the courier didn't knock until about 7:45."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand the frustration, Leo. Waiting nearly an hour for food that the app showed as delivered is a bad experience.\n\nThe $5.60 is the amount our late-delivery policy allows for an order this late. It's 20% of the food subtotal, and I can't add more beyond that. The courier's record shows the in-person handoff at 7:47 PM, so I can't treat this as an undelivered order.\n\nIf you still want more than this, I can connect you with a human specialist who can review the case. They'd follow up within 24 hours, but I can't promise what they'll decide. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Yes, please connect me with a specialist. I'd like someone to actually look at this. Also, I don't have the courier's record in front of me, but I was home from 7 and nothing came until about 7:45, so I'm not going to accept that the order was on time."
  },
  {
